{
  "_comment": [
    "Which scripting-API call covers each verb, and how the table is",
    "grouped. Authored: this is the design decision docs/scripting-verbs.md",
    "exists to record, and the one thing tools/verbdoc/verbdoc.py cannot",
    "read out of the tree.",
    "",
    "An empty facade means deliberately none - the store talking to",
    "itself - and it must have a matching entry in no_facade saying why.",
    "A verb with no entry here fails the script, which is the guard: a",
    "verb no client can reach is one nobody outside the workbench can use.",
    "",
    "A call spelled wb.<something>. names a namespace on the workbench, and",
    "tools/verbdoc/clients.py reads the three clients to find out which of",
    "those exist. One that none of them defines has to be listed in planned",
    "below, and the reference then prints the call marked as planned rather",
    "than as something a reader can call today. Without that a design note",
    "reads as an API: rf.* was mapped to wb.rf for five verbs and no client",
    "had an rf at all."
  ],
